  "name": "Gustling sprite",
  "notes": "Gustling, a round blue chick with a white face and belly, an orange beak and a head crest, drawn in the style of the monsters that walk around in GBA monster games: dark closed outline, 3 shades lit from the top-left. It is a Flying monster, so it is always in the air: its feet are tucked away and every frame flaps its wings. The body never moves inside the picture (same pixels, no bobbing up or down): only the wings, the eyes and the beak change. Seen from 8 directions: the front (down), the back (up), the side (right), the three-quarter views (down-right: the face turned right; up-right: the back turned right) and their left versions. The left views are drawn on their own, not mirrored by the engine: the shapes and the face mirror, but the shading stays lit from the top-left like every other view. Each view has the wings level (the plain frame), raised (_wings_up) and pushed down (_wings_down); the views that show the face also have a blink (wings level, eyes shut) and a strike (_lunge: wings down, beak open). In the three-quarter views the far wing is narrower, so it never covers the face or the beak tip. Every frame stays inside the 16x16 box with its outline closed, so nothing is ever cut at the edges. Too many frames to keep whole in video memory: it streams (only the frames on screen are loaded).",
